1
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:07,430
Babylon...

2
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:10,860
Wake up. Wake up.

3
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:25,220
Please, let me heal Babylon... 
let me cast divine sorcery on him!

4
00:00:31,010 --> 00:00:35,090
That's all right. 
Go get yourself some rest, miss.

5
00:00:35,330 --> 00:00:38,230
Please! Let me sing!

6
00:00:38,230 --> 00:00:39,590
Get a clue!

7
00:00:39,590 --> 00:00:40,670
Hey!

8
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:46,550
We were told Babylon was attacked 
by someone dressed like a pastor.

9
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:49,760
We can't trust anyone from the church!

10
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:22,800
I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince

11
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:22,800
so I Can Take My Time
Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season

12
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:43,560
Episode 18: Escher's Will

13
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:57,820
What blasphemy is this?!

14
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:09,500
I'm... sorry...

15
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:12,380
Anyone have any ideas?

16
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:14,630
I'm not sure what you're asking, but...

17
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:17,710
These are monsters.

18
00:03:17,710 --> 00:03:19,610
There're humans, too.

19
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:26,290
You can hear what's going on up 
in the church pretty clearly.

20
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:31,080
Considering he mentioned always 
hearing Escher's singing,

21
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:33,510
and his desire to have more security...

22
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:38,280
I believe this is that man's hideout.

23
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:43,160
He doesn't seem to be home, though. 
Do you think he'll be coming back?

24
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:47,660
I wouldn't count on it. 
Not after the scene he made above.

25
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:50,860
It's natural to assume this 
place would be discovered.

26
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:54,450
Sylpha! The way these are sewn together,

27
00:03:54,450 --> 00:03:56,860
they look just like the ghouls 
we fought in the sewer!

28
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:58,170
You're right.

29
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:01,900
Then what happened in the 
sewer was a part of it...

30
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,430
But what was he doing down here?

31
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:06,540
Look at that...

32
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:08,440
Synthesis.

33
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:12,420
This place has more of an 
alchemical lab than a sorcerous one.

34
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:15,660
Taking the cells of living organisms 
and then cultivating whole limbs,

35
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:16,950
before attaching them...

36
00:04:17,490 --> 00:04:20,190
It looks like his attempts 
to infuse wraiths into people

37
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:22,740
was a part of that research on synthesis.

38
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:26,960
All this was going on beneath the church?

39
00:04:26,960 --> 00:04:32,200
This makes it questionable if what we 
were fighting were genuine ghouls.

40
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:35,600
Creatures cobbled together
from various sources...

41
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:38,150
In other words, chimeras.

42
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:42,260
This is... horrible!

43
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:46,340
Toying with lives like this? 
He can't get away with it!

44
00:04:46,650 --> 00:04:53,230
The real question being, what did he intend 
on doing with the chimeras he was producing?

45
00:04:53,230 --> 00:04:55,820
Well, whatever it is, 
it's bound to be nasty.

46
00:04:55,820 --> 00:04:59,500
Yeah. Honestly, it's just so...

47
00:04:59,850 --> 00:05:01,170
Wepugnant!

48
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:01,860
Oh, ho...

49
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:01,860
Wepugnant?

50
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,120
Wepugnant?

51
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:06,870
Oh man, this guy sure is awful! Yep!

52
00:05:07,410 --> 00:05:09,440
<i>His sense of ethics might 
well be non-existent!</i>

53
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:12,370
<i>Which makes it likely that he's 
modified his own body a lot!</i>

54
00:05:12,630 --> 00:05:17,620
<i>I want to see it. I'd wager his own 
body is the culmination of all his study!</i>

55
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:20,670
Let's destroy this laboratory.

56
00:05:20,670 --> 00:05:22,000
Damn right.

57
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:24,500
This place is a nightmare!

58
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:27,010
You're really gonna wreck it? All of it?

59
00:05:27,010 --> 00:05:31,510
After a thorough search so we can inform 
Prince Albert of the details, of course.

60
00:05:31,870 --> 00:05:35,770
I'm surprised to learn you know so much 
about alchemy as well, Prince Lloyd.

61
00:05:36,260 --> 00:05:40,520
Nah! I just... read about it once...

62
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:40,530
Slither...

63
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:45,290
Drop!

64
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,900
Drop

65
00:05:55,710 --> 00:05:57,610
Is that a lamia?!

66
00:05:57,610 --> 00:06:00,660
The bastard has monsters wandering 
loose in this place?!

67
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:04,800
A... monster?

68
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,110
Don't kill her.

69
00:06:15,790 --> 00:06:18,800
That's the Air-class spell, Ventercier.

70
00:06:19,230 --> 00:06:20,320
Galilea.

71
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:21,070
On it.

72
00:06:21,410 --> 00:06:22,700
Arachnid Cocoon!

73
00:06:23,570 --> 00:06:24,570
Swerve

74
00:06:23,570 --> 00:06:24,570
Swerve!

75
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,890
Go, Ren.

76
00:06:26,890 --> 00:06:27,440
Okay.

77
00:06:32,390 --> 00:06:35,420
A magic barrier? She can use 
that kind of technique?

78
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:37,700
This is gonna take a while.

79
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:38,710
<i>No.</i>

80
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:42,830
Kneel! Kneel!

81
00:06:44,770 --> 00:06:46,750
<i>He got the demons with this one.</i>

82
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:50,600
Mana focus... Recitation Loop!

83
00:06:51,730 --> 00:06:53,850
Kneel! Kneel! Kneel!

84
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:00,400
Wow!

85
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:06,100
With a single attack...

86
00:07:06,310 --> 00:07:09,110
With a power like that, 
I'm glad you're on our side.

87
00:07:09,110 --> 00:07:14,110
Your cursed speech has gotten way stronger 
since you've gained control over it, Crow.

88
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:13,620
You used me as
a decoy, didn't you?

89
00:07:12,910 --> 00:07:14,120
Sorry

90
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:17,230
Now, take a closer look. 
It's just like I thought.

91
00:07:17,630 --> 00:07:21,550
She wasn't cultivated in here. She's human.

92
00:07:22,590 --> 00:07:24,540
Even if half of her is a monster.

93
00:07:25,190 --> 00:07:28,010
Synthesis experiments on living humans?

94
00:07:28,270 --> 00:07:29,920
Who's this guy think he is?!

95
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:37,230
What do we do? What can we do for her?

96
00:07:41,450 --> 00:07:42,240
Kneel...

97
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,030
Wait!

98
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,550
Please, wait!

99
00:07:48,670 --> 00:07:52,020
It's okay. You don't have to be afraid.

100
00:07:52,610 --> 00:07:54,530
We're all here to help.

101
00:07:54,850 --> 00:07:57,530
Escher, watch out! If you get too close—

102
00:08:03,910 --> 00:08:04,920
Escher!

103
00:08:06,730 --> 00:08:08,540
<i>That makes sense.</i>

104
00:08:09,330 --> 00:08:10,680
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

105
00:08:13,770 --> 00:08:16,430
<i>It's only natural you'd be scared.</i>

106
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:20,840
<i>I've been scared out of 
my mind this whole time.</i>

107
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:22,720
<i>And feeling powerless.</i>

108
00:08:23,310 --> 00:08:28,730
<i>What can someone like me... even do?</i>

109
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:57,260
This melody...

110
00:09:19,420 --> 00:09:20,250
Hey.

111
00:09:21,390 --> 00:09:24,300
How long has she been singing?

112
00:09:27,110 --> 00:09:28,670
The entire time. It's been over twelve hours.

113
00:09:29,740 --> 00:09:31,510
That's crazy!

114
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:35,340
She isn't even casting divine sorcery!

115
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:38,690
She's run through all of her mana already!

116
00:09:38,690 --> 00:09:43,520
So how is she still upright? Still singing?

117
00:09:43,830 --> 00:09:44,820
This girl...

118
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:49,060
<i>She's amazing.</i>

119
00:09:49,890 --> 00:09:51,820
<i>And her singing...</i>

120
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:08,370
<i>I remember. I could hear it all the time...</i>

121
00:10:08,370 --> 00:10:09,720
<i>This singing.</i>

122
00:10:11,190 --> 00:10:14,040
<i>Coming down from that pitch black ceiling...</i>

123
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:15,370
<i>The same song.</i>

124
00:10:16,570 --> 00:10:21,600
<i>Even he would stop moving when he heard it.</i>

125
00:10:22,850 --> 00:10:23,980
<i>I remember.</i>

126
00:10:24,390 --> 00:10:27,900
<i>When it felt like the monster was 
going to take over my mind...</i>

127
00:10:28,330 --> 00:10:30,160
<i>I would hear this.</i>

128
00:10:30,830 --> 00:10:34,150
<i>The voice of the person who
kept me from losing myself...</i>

129
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:41,110
I'm sorry.

130
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:45,150
Um, I...

131
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:48,830
I'm...

132
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:53,750
I'm human! I'm sorry!

133
00:11:01,790 --> 00:11:04,750
I'm sorry, too.

134
00:11:05,590 --> 00:11:08,120
You were so close by...

135
00:11:09,970 --> 00:11:12,440
but I never noticed.

136
00:11:30,130 --> 00:11:32,960
I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince

137
00:11:30,130 --> 00:11:32,960
so I Can Take My Time
Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season

138
00:11:33,290 --> 00:11:36,210
Prince Albert's here!

139
00:11:36,670 --> 00:11:39,720
A chimera laboratory beneath the church.

140
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:44,440
As much as I'd like to hunt down 
the culprit as soon as possible...

141
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:48,510
I'm sorry I couldn't be of more help.

142
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:52,230
Amnesia bad enough to make 
you forget your own name...

143
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:55,240
That sounds like a side-effect of 
the chimerazation experiments.

144
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:59,390
I've got a good idea, though. 
You probably used to be an adventurer!

145
00:11:59,390 --> 00:12:02,230
That makes sense, 
since she could use sorcery.

146
00:12:02,230 --> 00:12:04,560
But even if I knew my identity,

147
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:07,490
with my body like this, living a normal 
life is out of the question...

148
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:13,720
Relax! We're from Lordost Island, and it's a 
place where folks like you can live happy lives.

149
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:14,900
Come on down!

150
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:16,750
We'll make a long skirt for you!

151
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:18,340
Everyone...

152
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,010
Just who exactly is this 
mysterious pastor, though?

153
00:12:24,260 --> 00:12:27,760
Oh, I found this in the laboratory.

154
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:30,390
Do you think it'll be any help?

155
00:12:30,930 --> 00:12:33,530
That's certainly an old-looking rosary.

156
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:37,980
I'm not sure it belongs to the person you've 
been calling the mysterious pastor,

157
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:40,150
but I do have faint memories of him.

158
00:12:40,150 --> 00:12:43,260
I think he... hates the gods.

159
00:12:44,910 --> 00:12:49,030
I've got something for you, 
while we're on the subject.

160
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:53,540
Those are the notes from the lab...

161
00:12:53,540 --> 00:12:55,470
With the research data!

162
00:12:55,470 --> 00:12:59,040
<i>He snatched them the second he heard 
the lab was going to be destroyed.</i>

163
00:12:59,470 --> 00:13:03,050
Lloyd, you can't! Having her look 
through this sort of thing...

164
00:13:03,270 --> 00:13:05,810
She can always burn it, if she wants to.

165
00:13:07,090 --> 00:13:11,800
But this data is the only lead we have 
in turning you fully human again.

166
00:13:12,450 --> 00:13:15,590
Your body is functioning 
thanks to a combination

167
00:13:15,590 --> 00:13:19,260
of mana signatures too complex for 
even me to grasp at a glance.

168
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:22,340
You're the only one who can learn this data,

169
00:13:22,340 --> 00:13:25,830
compare it to your situation, and figure 
out how to change your body back.

170
00:13:25,830 --> 00:13:27,980
Dispose of it, and put it behind you,

171
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:30,700
or push forward, without looking 
away from your trauma.

172
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,400
It's your choice.

173
00:13:38,750 --> 00:13:42,970
Thank you! I'll do what I can!

174
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:53,850
All right, and we'll help however we can.

175
00:13:53,850 --> 00:13:56,470
And that being the case, 
let's give you a name.

176
00:13:56,480 --> 00:14:06,240
Please enter a name.

177
00:13:56,480 --> 00:14:06,240
It can't be changed later.

178
00:13:56,480 --> 00:14:06,240
Name

179
00:13:57,100 --> 00:14:00,650
Make it something auspicious 
sounding, Prince Lloyd!

180
00:14:00,650 --> 00:14:02,050
P-Please.

181
00:14:02,050 --> 00:14:06,230
A name full of hope that she'll 
be human again someday!

182
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:08,230
Then...

183
00:14:08,230 --> 00:14:11,460
How about Lami? 
Because it sounds like lamia.

184
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:12,370
Lami

185
00:14:13,330 --> 00:14:16,630
<i>Did she go back to the castle already?</i>

186
00:14:16,630 --> 00:14:19,530
<i>Saria... Saria!</i>

187
00:14:19,530 --> 00:14:21,120
Saria!

188
00:14:21,410 --> 00:14:22,380
What?

189
00:14:22,650 --> 00:14:26,250
Saria?! What are you still 
doing at the church?

190
00:14:26,520 --> 00:14:29,160
I was eating some of Macaron's babylons.

191
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:31,510
As a break from my recital practice.

192
00:14:33,270 --> 00:14:36,260
Would you like some, Escher? 
Some of <i>Babylon's macarons.</i>

193
00:14:37,770 --> 00:14:39,610
I'm sorry, Saria.

194
00:14:40,330 --> 00:14:43,570
Babylon... I'm going to sing after all.

195
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,890
I want to!

196
00:14:46,430 --> 00:14:50,540
Because it's the only thing I'm good at!

197
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:54,000
Very good. Let's make it a big show.

198
00:14:55,390 --> 00:14:57,220
For the Great Advent Festival...

199
00:14:58,040 --> 00:15:00,550
Tousle Tousle

200
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,430
The Advent Festival must be canceled.

201
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:09,070
Whaaat?!

202
00:15:04,170 --> 00:15:05,050
Good boy.

203
00:15:09,070 --> 00:15:11,590
Man, the gang's all here now, huh?

204
00:15:11,590 --> 00:15:15,610
Albert, we can't cancel, no matter what!

205
00:15:15,610 --> 00:15:18,460
Well, the thing is, Saria...

206
00:15:18,850 --> 00:15:21,860
<i>I notice she gets his name right.</i>

207
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:26,210
After what Lami said about the 
mysterious pastor having some grudge

208
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:27,970
against the Church and the gods...

209
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:28,740
Right!

210
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:31,240
Everyone, this is incredible!

211
00:15:31,490 --> 00:15:34,170
Look how funny he looks after 
I put the necklace on him!

212
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,210
You're right!

213
00:15:39,370 --> 00:15:41,370
It won't come off!

214
00:15:42,790 --> 00:15:43,500
Bop

215
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:43,500
Bop

216
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:43,500
Bop

217
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:50,130
We can assume he hates Escher's singing, 
which is to say, hymns.

218
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:54,360
The real issue is what 
exactly he intended to do,

219
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:56,680
considering the scale of the 
laboratory he had built.

220
00:15:57,120 --> 00:16:00,640
I'd probably raise all kinds of 
hell at the Great Advent Festival.

221
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:03,390
I think I'd try and kill the Pope.

222
00:16:04,770 --> 00:16:06,030
Yay!

223
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:09,850
That sounds really likely... 
which means we really ought to cancel...

224
00:16:09,850 --> 00:16:11,720
But how do I make that kind of announcement?

225
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:14,530
There's going to be so much backlash, 
no matter what I do...

226
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:18,780
There's an additional 
complication to consider.

227
00:16:19,110 --> 00:16:22,670
Regarding the rosary that Lami found...

228
00:16:22,670 --> 00:16:24,280
Wait, where did it go?

229
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:26,800
Katarina had it a second ago.

230
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:28,800
Over here, woof...

231
00:16:27,170 --> 00:16:28,550
<i>Over here, woof.</i>

232
00:16:28,910 --> 00:16:33,040
If this actually did belong 
to the mysterious pastor,

233
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,050
things are even worse than we imagined.

234
00:16:35,050 --> 00:16:38,370
I have a silver rosary, too.

235
00:16:38,370 --> 00:16:41,920
It... matches Babylon's.

236
00:16:42,250 --> 00:16:45,450
The one that I saw him with 
was practically brand new.

237
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:48,670
Maybe he needed a new one, 
after losing the one she found.

238
00:16:48,670 --> 00:16:51,810
Even if that's the case, 
I'm not seeing the problem.

239
00:16:52,130 --> 00:16:54,760
Most rosaries are made from silver.

240
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:58,130
But this one is solid gold.

241
00:16:58,130 --> 00:17:00,750
Right. A solid gold rosary.

242
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:04,320
There are only twelve people 
allowed to carry those...

243
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:09,740
Including the Pope, the twelve bishops 
who oversee the central church.

244
00:17:09,990 --> 00:17:13,220
You're saying one of the 
twelve bishops is the bad guy?!

245
00:17:14,020 --> 00:17:15,670
That's absurd!

246
00:17:15,670 --> 00:17:19,140
These are great holy people, 
they would never do such a thing!

247
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:20,490
Yeah, that's right...

248
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:20,900
For one thing, none of them resemble him!

249
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:27,890
No. Based on Babylon's description, 
he can likely change his form freely.

250
00:17:29,270 --> 00:17:34,380
Th-Then suppose the rosary is a forgery, 
or was stolen from one of the bishops...

251
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:38,420
Whatever the case, there's no way that 
one of them could be the culprit!

252
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:42,170
Oh, Babylon made Escher sad.

253
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:46,910
You suck! Go get your soul cleansed 
with some purification magic.

254
00:17:47,230 --> 00:17:49,380
Then we'll have a nice Babylon!

255
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:52,340
Squeak!!!

256
00:17:51,290 --> 00:17:52,340
Squeak!

257
00:17:52,550 --> 00:17:54,040
I can sing!

258
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:57,290
Don't! I don't need purification—

259
00:17:58,670 --> 00:17:59,960
Luxa.

260
00:18:01,450 --> 00:18:06,580
He didn't need a ritual 
to use divine sorcery.

261
00:18:07,110 --> 00:18:08,430
He had a pass.

262
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:16,550
<i>Ever since Prince Lloyd arranged it for us, 
we've been taking it for granted...</i>

263
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:20,260
Usually, divine sorcery requires a ritual.

264
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:23,190
Like Escher's singing, or dancing,

265
00:18:23,190 --> 00:18:25,940
which makes it magic that's a bit 
more complicated to execute.

266
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:31,460
That makes it certain, then.

267
00:18:31,460 --> 00:18:36,960
Having a pass that makes divine 
sorcery possible without a ritual...

268
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:44,220
It could only be the 12 bishops.

269
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:55,990
I found a chess board!

270
00:18:55,990 --> 00:18:57,340
I wanna play!

271
00:18:57,340 --> 00:18:59,970
Hey, I have one of those—

272
00:18:59,970 --> 00:19:01,620
Shut up before you complicate things.

273
00:19:03,030 --> 00:19:04,460
Is that all true?

274
00:19:04,460 --> 00:19:07,630
Broadly, but not quite.

275
00:19:07,630 --> 00:19:11,940
I only gave access to a 
pass to the Pope, Guitane.

276
00:19:11,940 --> 00:19:15,440
The other eleven individuals 
are people he trusts.

277
00:19:16,650 --> 00:19:20,680
Similar to the relationship between Prince 
Lloyd and the Lordost Island people.

278
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:22,870
I trust you, Prince Lloyd!

279
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:25,060
I endorse these guys.

280
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:26,860
Then I trust them too!

281
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:30,890
Rare to hear you having anything 
good to say about a dude...

282
00:19:30,890 --> 00:19:33,650
Then again, I guess Prince Lloyd is one, too.

283
00:19:34,130 --> 00:19:37,020
And Guitane is a fair comparison.

284
00:19:39,910 --> 00:19:44,220
Given the Church's total rejection 
of Babylon's testimony,

285
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:49,740
I doubt they'll be willing to cancel the 
Advent Festival no matter what we tell them.

286
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:50,630
<i>Oute</i>!

287
00:19:50,630 --> 00:19:52,180
Maybe if we were playing shogi!

288
00:19:52,180 --> 00:19:55,940
And more importantly, if the enemy really 
has infiltrated the central church,

289
00:19:53,470 --> 00:19:55,010
Good point...

290
00:19:55,940 --> 00:20:00,800
then His Holiness' life would still be in 
danger regardless of any cancellation.

291
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:05,310
True. And most pressingly, there's very 
little time left until the festival.

292
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:13,410
If the mysterious pastor is 
among these eleven people...

293
00:20:13,410 --> 00:20:17,290
We'll have to separate the Pope from 
his bishops on the day in question,

294
00:20:17,290 --> 00:20:22,060
while we watch them closely, 
under the pretext of providing security.

295
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:28,940
That should at least allow us to 
prevent the Pope's assassination

296
00:20:28,940 --> 00:20:31,170
on the day of the Great Advent Festival.

297
00:20:31,670 --> 00:20:34,620
That might be the only 
option we really have.

298
00:20:35,210 --> 00:20:40,380
I'll do what I can, but given the situation, 
we can't turn to the Adventurer's Guild.

299
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:43,210
Those of us here are the only 
ones we can really trust.

300
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:45,910
If you notice anything 
suspicious with the bishops,

301
00:20:45,910 --> 00:20:48,150
use your own judgment to try and secure them.

302
00:20:48,150 --> 00:20:51,200
We need to make sure the Great Advent 
Festival ends safely, no matter what!

303
00:20:57,270 --> 00:20:58,150
Wait right there.

304
00:21:00,150 --> 00:21:01,860
Bishop Anastasia.

305
00:21:02,730 --> 00:21:05,310
What's that letter you have there?

306
00:21:05,310 --> 00:21:10,210
Well, it's... a message from 
the second prince, Albert.

307
00:21:10,670 --> 00:21:11,940
Let me see it.

308
00:21:11,940 --> 00:21:16,070
But I was told to give it 
directly to His Holiness...

309
00:21:23,730 --> 00:21:26,050
B-Bishop Anastasia?

310
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:52,100
This is a letter sent from the 
second prince to the pope.

311
00:21:53,450 --> 00:21:57,330
He wants to inspect the church's facilities,

312
00:21:57,330 --> 00:22:00,200
with the Pope and the bishops 
in separate groups.

313
00:22:00,430 --> 00:22:05,210
I see. Intel gained from the 
artificial lamia, I presume.

314
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:10,570
Yes. It's likely that underground facility 
was destroyed by the second prince.

315
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:15,470
But from the contents of the message, 
it seems he didn't learn much—

316
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:22,060
There was nothing left of Civil War, 
apart from this arm.

317
00:22:22,610 --> 00:22:27,270
Granted, his actual cause of death was 
the Luma Maxima I provided him with...

318
00:22:27,270 --> 00:22:30,070
But his left arm had already been severed.

319
00:22:30,070 --> 00:22:35,800
It's likely he was engaged in battle with 
something even he couldn't react to.

320
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:38,120
As for what that could be...

321
00:22:38,620 --> 00:22:42,120
I may have overlooked something 
rather significant.

322
00:22:44,820 --> 00:22:50,500
However, nothing the second prince 
could concoct at this point

323
00:22:50,500 --> 00:22:53,130
should pose any kind of problem.

324
00:22:55,780 --> 00:23:02,270
If he thinks that shutting down a mere branch 
laboratory could impede me even the slightest...

325
00:23:02,270 --> 00:23:06,960
No. Even if he knows exactly 
what I intend to do...

326
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:08,530
it won't matter.

327
00:23:12,790 --> 00:23:15,270
The time has come.

328
00:23:17,030 --> 00:23:23,040
There is no one who can 
stop us at this point.

329
00:23:26,120 --> 00:23:27,250
Now...

330
00:23:27,730 --> 00:23:29,330
Let the curtain rise...

331
00:23:30,610 --> 00:23:32,940
on the Great Advent Festival.

332
00:23:35,630 --> 00:23:39,030
<i>The mastermind is among the twelve bishops?!</i>

333
00:23:39,030 --> 00:23:41,550
<i>My vases... I need to polish 
my vases to calm down!</i>

334
00:23:42,030 --> 00:23:44,400
<i>Next time, Episode 19:</i>

335
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:46,170
<i>"The Great Advent Festival."</i>

336
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:49,990
Episode 19

337
